PHASE T — the search's UNMEASURED hypothesis, measured as far as this instrument allows.
   The search says: every armed move loses tail uprightness, and it did not measure why.
   The servo owns the legs only while the TRACK runs; the 50 policy tail ticks put them
   back on HOME + policy action. The 'hold' tail does NOT: rig3 freezes the servo's LAST
   COMMAND on the ten slots it owns. So policy-tail vs hold-tail uprightness on the same
   file, at cell 0 (rise 60 mm, drop 0.120, friction x1.0), separates the two.
   best_r3_vault_60mm.json            servoArmed=false  policy tail 50/50 honest=true  |  hold tail 13/50 honest=false  |  delta -37  stable(hold)=false
   best_r5_servoland_kcore_60mm.json  servoArmed=true  policy tail 25/50 honest=true  |  hold tail 5/50 honest=false  |  delta -20  stable(hold)=false
   best_r5_servo_60mm.json            servoArmed=true  policy tail 15/50 honest=true  |  hold tail 0/50 honest=false  |  delta -15  stable(hold)=false
